## Step 3: Apply Computational Thinking Skills
| **Sub-problem** | **CT Skill** | **Proposed Solution** |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Students spend too much time deciding what to order, which slows down the queue. | Abstraction | Provide a simple menu showing the available food, prices, and short descriptions to help students decide quickly. |
| Payment process takes too long and is prone to errors | Algorithm Design | Create a step-by-step system that calculates the total price, accepts the payment, and gives correct change. | 
| Canteen does not have real-time way to track food inventory | Pattern Recognition | Track the quantity of each food item and give a warning when the stock reaches a low level. | 
| The servic process if disorganized | Decomposition | Separare the process into ordering, payment, and pickup stages so students can follow an organized flow. | 

